{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed stitch task (Task ID: 5478) to implement srd072 requirements R3.1 through R3.4 for `cmd/od` (octal dump utility) in the go-unix-utils project. The specific requirements are:\n   - R3.1: `-w[N]` or `--width[=N]` to set bytes per output line (default 16; 32 when `-w` given without value)\n   - R3.2: Traditional short option aliases: `-b` = `-t o1`, `-c` = `-t c`, `-d` = `-t u2`, `-o` = `-t o2`, `-s` = `-t d2`, `-x` = `-t x2`\n   - R3.3: Duplicate line suppression with `*` on a line by itself\n   - R3.4: `-v` or `--output-duplicates` to disable `*` duplicate suppression\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/od/main.go` and `cmd/od/od_test.go`. Must use differential testing against `god` (GNU od from Homebrew).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`god`) using `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for byte-identical output comparison\n   - Octal dump formatting with configurable type specifiers, address radixes, and output widths\n   - Duplicate line suppression (replacing repeated output lines with `*`)\n   - Traditional POSIX short-flag aliases for type specifiers\n   - Go module build: `go build -o bin/od ./cmd/od/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd072-od.yaml`\n     - Full SRD defining all requirements R1-R4 for the od utility\n     - R3 group (lines 42-53) defines width control, traditional options, duplicate suppression, and verbose mode\n     - Non-goals: no `--strings` (-S) and no `--endian`\n\n   - `cmd/od/main.go` (388 lines)\n     - **R3 features already implemented in existing code:**\n     - `options` struct (line 22-30) has `outputWidth int`, `verbose bool` fields\n     - `main()` (line 51-71): sets default `outputWidth = 16` at line 62\n     - `dump()` (lines 96-131): implements duplicate suppression with `prevLine`, `duplicating` bool, `equalBytes()` check, and `fmt.Println(\"*\")` at line 109. Verbose mode check at line 107: `!opts.verbose`\n     - `equalBytes()` (lines 345-355): byte-by-byte comparison for duplicate detection\n\n   - `cmd/od/parse.go` (273 lines)\n     - **R3 features already implemented in existing code:**\n     - `parseLongFlag()`: handles `--width=N` (line 59), `--width` without value sets 32 (lines 61-63), `--output-duplicates` sets verbose (lines 53-54)\n     - `parseShortFlags()`: handles `-v` (lines 85-86), `-w` (lines 87-89), calls `traditionalFlag()` for `-b/-c/-d/-o/-s/-x` (lines 91-93)\n     - `traditionalFlag()` (lines 101-117): maps `-b`→`o1`, `-c`→`c1`, `-d`→`u2`, `-o`→`o2`, `-s`→`d2`, `-x`→`x2`\n     - `parseShortWidth()` (lines 119-131): handles `-wN` inline or `-w N` with next arg, defaults to 32\n     - `parseWidth()` (lines 180-193): parses width integer value\n\n   - `cmd/od/od_test.go` (146 lines)\n     - **Missing R3 test cases** — existing tests only cover R1-R2 functionality\n     - Has test helpers: `bytes16()`, `typeSpecTests()`, `multiTypeTests()`, `addressRadixTests()`, `skipAndReadTests()`, `stdinAndFileTests()`\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"god\")` with skip pattern\n     - Has `discardStderr` normalizer for error cases\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only file reading was performed before the task was interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Discovered that all four R3 requirements appear to already be implemented in the existing `cmd/od/main.go` and `cmd/od/parse.go` code from prior tasks.\n   - The key gap is that `cmd/od/od_test.go` has NO test cases covering R3 features (width, traditional flags, duplicate suppression, verbose mode).\n   - The task therefore primarily requires adding comprehensive differential test cases and verifying the existing implementation works correctly.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full stitch task prompt with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), context (Task 5478: [stitch] cmd/od: srd072 R3.1-R3.4), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — Instructing to provide only a text summary without any tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Add differential test cases to `cmd/od/od_test.go` covering:\n     - R3.1: Width control tests (`-w`, `-w32`, `-w8`, `--width=8`, `--width` without value)\n     - R3.2: Traditional short option tests (`-b`, `-c`, `-d`, `-o`, `-s`, `-x`)\n     - R3.3: Duplicate suppression tests (repeated data showing `*`)\n     - R3.4: Verbose mode tests (`-v`, `--output-duplicates` disabling `*`)\n   - Verify existing R3 implementation correctness by running `go build ./cmd/od/` and `go test ./cmd/od/ -count=1`\n   - Verify `go vet ./cmd/od/` passes\n   - Fix any bugs found in the R3 implementation\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all four relevant files (`srd072-od.yaml`, `cmd/od/main.go`, `cmd/od/od_test.go`, `cmd/od/parse.go`) and was about to begin implementation when the summary was requested. My analysis revealed that the R3 functionality is already coded in main.go and parse.go, but test coverage for R3 is completely absent from od_test.go.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Add test helper functions and test cases to `cmd/od/od_test.go` for R3.1-R3.4, following the existing test patterns (helper functions returning `[]testutils.DiffTest` slices). Specifically:\n   - Add `widthTests()` function for R3.1 tests\n   - Add `traditionalFlagTests()` function for R3.2 tests  \n   - Add `duplicateSuppressionTests()` function for R3.3 tests (needs repeated data input)\n   - Add `verboseTests()` function for R3.4 tests\n   - Append all to the `tests` slice in `TestDiff`\n   - Then run `go vet ./cmd/od/` and `go test ./cmd/od/ -count=1` to verify\n\n   The task description states: \"Implement srd072 requirement R3.1 per the SRD specification\" through R3.4, with acceptance criteria requiring both implementation in main.go AND differential test cases in od_test.go.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5478/3e72a613-4699-4d02-8229-895fbf456266.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e72a613-4699-4d02-8229-895fbf456266","uuid":"a3776091-8fd0-4112-9a0d-6d424673e6f3","timestamp":"2026-05-22T23:40:57.358Z","isSynthetic":true}
